As the war in Iran rages on and fuel costs soar, an already difficult post-pandemic touring landscape has become nearly impossible for working musicians. Yet despite high costs, more artists are out on tour than ever — creating fierce competition in the marketplace.&nbsp;

To help offset those high costs, artists and promoters are getting creative with their approach.&nbsp;

